# clang-tidy configuration for lunar_simulator.
#
# This is a real static-analysis pass, not a certification claim: per
# CPP_CODING_STANDARD.md Section 15.4, clang-tidy is NOT a certified MISRA
# C++ checker. Any compliance document that cites a clang-tidy run must
# state that distinction explicitly rather than imply certified coverage.
#
# Scope: report-only (WarningsAsErrors is empty) across the whole repo.
# Magic-number checks are disabled because the pre-existing
# test_kalman_math.cpp style already uses bare numeric literals in
# assertions, and modernize-use-trailing-return-type is disabled as a
# stylistic choice this repo does not follow.
#
# cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index is disabled
# repo-wide, not suppressed per-site, because it fires ~38 times across
# feature_tracking/ on the exact same structural pattern: a runtime
# std::array index already bounded by an initialize()-time-validated
# range or a fixed loop limit (e.g. a pyramid level index, a window
# offset). Switching every one of those hot-loop accesses to .at() would
# add a bounds check per pixel/iteration, undermining the real-time
# margin restored by CMakeLists.txt's RelWithDebInfo default (see
# CLAUDE.md) for no safety benefit the surrounding loop structure doesn't
# already provide -- and 38 near-identical NOLINT comments would be
# noise, not an auditable trail. Raw-pointer-arithmetic checks are
# treated differently and deliberately left ENABLED (not
# blanket-suppressed): ImageView::at() (feature_tracking/objects/
# ImageView.h) is the ONE site in this codebase using unchecked pointer
# arithmetic by design (see docs/compliance/feature_tracking/
# DEVIATION_LOG.md DEV-FT-003), so it is suppressed per-site with a
# justified `// NOLINT(...)` instead, keeping that checker maximally
# strict everywhere else.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-constant-array-index

WarningsAsErrors: ''

HeaderFilterRegex: 'src/.*'

FormatStyle: none
